diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 3a5f273..8b44fca 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -37,7 +37,7 @@ Native client for iTa'leem (IIUM Moodle) using Moodle's mobile web-service API,
 - The home-screen icon follows the theme (Dark, Light and Terminal each have their own). iOS shows its own "You have changed the icon" notice when it changes; apps can't hide it
 - Terminal: near-black with a green tint, neon green accent, monospaced font, a green glow around cards and prominent text, faint CRT scanlines over the app (off when Reduce Transparency is on), and an occasional glitch (text jumps and splits into red and cyan ghosts for about 0.3 s every few seconds; off when Reduce Motion is on) and green-tinted course covers
 - Retro: old arcade look. Black with dark olive tiles, yellow accent, almost square cards with a thick outline and a hard offset block shadow, monospaced font, yellow-tinted course covers and a chunky 64x64 pixel-art yellow app icon. Headings and navigation titles use the built-in "iTaleem Pixel" font (`Fonts/`, regenerated with `Tools/make_pixel_font.py`, which needs `pip install fonttools`)
-- Red Dead Redemption 2: Rockstar-poster look. Black and red, off-white text, cards with the usual rounded shape, a dark-red outline and a torn-paper red banner on top, faded red grunge stars over the page, a dark vignette and grain, red-and-black course covers and a red icon. One custom font for everything, 20% bigger than the other themes' text: capitals are Chinese Rocks (Typodermic Fonts, the game's lettering), small letters are Tavern (Oleg Voznyy). `Tools/make_rdr_font.py` builds it into `Fonts/ChineseRocksPlus-Regular.ttf` from the originals in `Tools/source`, redraws `&`, brackets and braces (from Staatliches, OFL) and adds check marks, bullets, arrows and shapes, so no symbol falls back to the system font. Check the licences before publishing the app
+- Red Dead Redemption 2: Rockstar-poster look. Black and red, off-white text, cards with the usual rounded shape, a dark-red outline and a torn-paper red banner on top, faded red grunge stars over the page, a dark vignette and grain, red-and-black course covers and a red icon. One custom font for everything, 20% bigger than the other themes' text: capitals are Chinese Rocks (Typodermic Fonts, the game's lettering), small letters are Tavern (Oleg Voznyy). `Tools/make_rdr_font.py` builds it into `Fonts/ChineseRocksPlus-Regular.ttf` from the originals in `Tools/source`, redraws `&`, brackets and braces (from Staatliches, OFL) and adds check marks, bullets, arrows and shapes, so no symbol falls back to the system font. Check the licences before publishing the app. Headings, tab strips, the tab bar, navigation titles and the Sync now button use Chinese Rocks Rg (`Fonts/ChineseRocksCaps-Regular.ttf`, all capitals, built by `Tools/make_rocks_caps.py`; only `&`, brackets and braces are redrawn from Staatliches, like in the Plus font)
 - Course covers follow the theme: bright pastel default covers and undimmed photos in Light, dimmed photos in the dark themes
 - Each theme is a `Palette` in `Theme.swift` plus an entry in `Themes.swift`, and an icon set in `Sources/Assets.xcassets` (`AppIcon-<Name>`, listed in `project.yml`)
 
